          "chapterId": "c-0003",
          "paragraph": 539,
          "paragraphId": "p-000540",
          "excerpt": "…were followed by a very long silence, broken only by an occasional exclamation of “Hjckrrh!” from the Gryphon, and the constant heavy sobbing of the Mock Turtle. Alice was very nearly getting up and saying, “Thank you, sir, for your interesting story,” but she could not help thinking there _must_ be more to c…"
