          "chapterId": "c-0003",
          "paragraph": 676,
          "paragraphId": "p-000677",
          "excerpt": "The first witness was the Hatter. He came in with a teacup in one hand and a piece of bread-and-butter in the other. “I beg pardon, your Majesty,” he began, “for bringing these in: but I hadn’t quite finished my tea when I was sent for.”"
        },
