          "chapterId": "c-0003",
          "paragraph": 697,
          "paragraphId": "p-000698",
          "excerpt": "“I’m a poor man, your Majesty,” the Hatter began, in a trembling voice, “—and I hadn’t begun my tea—not above a week or so—and what with the bread-and-butter getting so thin—and t…"
        },
        {
          "chapter": "Chapter III: A Caucus-Race and a Long Tale",
          "chapterId": "c-0003",
          "paragraph": 711,
          "paragraphId": "p-000712",
          "excerpt": "The miserable Hatter dropped his teacup and bread-and-butter, and went down on one knee. “I’m a poor man, your Majesty,” he began."
